meta {
  name: List Devices
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/devices
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists all of the devices in an org — the List Devices endpoint, with no filters applied here.

  **Parameters**: none set on this example, though the endpoint supports optional query filters
  such as `personId`, `workspaceId`, `locationId`, and `mac` (see the Hardware Inventory folder for
  filtered variants of this same request).

  **Usage**: Good starting point to see every registered device and note its `id` / `callingDeviceId`
  / `webexDeviceId` for use in other requests (e.g. "Get Device Members", Phone Control).

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/devices/list-devices

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
